  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="694f-c34a-36db-a697" name="Alexander &amp; his Successors (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>ALEXANDER &amp; HIS SUCCESSORS ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.16-17).
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Battle Standard. Cavalry up to half the points; Infantry at least a quarter; Special Troops &amp; Allies up to half, with one artillery piece or scythed chariot per 500 points and one elephant per 1,000 points.
Allies: allied units can be taken from the Barbarian, Persian, Indian, Cataphract and Ancient Greek army lists (not built here: make a separate small roster for allies).
Wedge formation, the staff sling (treated as a crossbow) and the phalanx are explained in the rules.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Special Troops &amp; Allies: up to 50%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
